  "details": "Since I hear the devs are planning on updating standard-lite, I have an important suggestion. Since VRAM usage is super important (and doubly so on Android since it shares system RAM), I'd like to like to suggest some improvements to help creators optimize more effectively.\n\nCurrently Standard-lite inherits much of its format from Standard. However I think it would be much more advantageous if some of the texture channels were chosen more wisely. \n\nSo for reference the current setup:\n\nAlbedo: R,G,B\n\nMetallic/Smoothness: R, A\n\nOpacity: G\n\nDetail Mask: A\n\nThis leaves us with a wasted Blue channel on the metallic map, and the detail mask bizarrely all alone on an alpha channel.\n\nIf we switch the Detail Mask to the Blue channel we could utilize that extra channel.\n\nAlternatively, an Emission Mask slot could be added which uses a Blue channel, so we could pack that in with the Metallic packed texture, that might be best if you want the full MOES standard. And that could save an entire RGB emission texture if you don't need more than one color.",
